.TH PATH_IS_ABSOLUTE_SA 3
.SH NAME
path_is_absolute_sa \- check if a stralloc path is absolute
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "int path_is_absolute_sa(const stralloc* " p ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_is_absolute_sa
checks whether the path contained in the
.B stralloc
structure
.I p
is an absolute path.
.PP
This function acts as a wrapper around
.BR path_is_absolute_b (3),
using the data buffer
.I p->s
and length
.I p->len
to perform the check according to the platform-specific rules for absolute paths.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.TP
.B 1
The path is absolute.
.TP
.B 0
The path is relative.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_is_absolute_b (3),
.BR path_is_absolute (3),
.BR stralloc (3)